A||||13||Formula88||Live from Williamsburg!||||6||
Z||000000||Formula88||08-03-2001||01:12 AM||||Well, LZeitgeist and I brought "The Twins" to Williamsburg this morning.  We got here about 3 this afternoon, and after finally getting in our room, the washing and waxing could begin.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I finally got to meet some of the people from the Forum for the first time; FieroLisa, Chris Moore, Skitime...a few others.  We've got LZeitgeist's Mavica, so we'll be posting some pics over the weekend.  As soon as PIP finishes downloading to my laptop, that is. <P>To be continued....||||reg||6
Z||000001||k2m4||08-03-2001||04:06 PM||||Once again i am soooooooooo freakin jeolous im going to cry! i wish i was there ...sniff sniff i cant see my screen....<BR>k<P>------------------<BR>Kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||9
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||08-03-2001||05:02 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I was intending to go but spent too much money and couldn't fit the trip into my budget  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Now I am wishing I would have gone broke and got to go to the show. Carlisle and buying my 88 GT was heavy on my wallet. I want lots of pics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||9
Z||000003||Formula88||08-04-2001||05:32 PM||||Ok, finally back on the Forum!  Now I can get some pics in here.<P>Here's me & LZeitgeist when we first arrived on Thurs. afternoon...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Day_1_Small_1.jpg">   <P>Friday's cruise through Historic Williamsburg was pretty awesome:<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-008f_2.jpg">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/The_Twins_at_Yorktown_small_1.JPG">   <P>Friday evening, after the cruise and some more car cleaning, the Fieros get tucked in for the night...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tucked_in.jpg"> <P>Saturday morning,  The Stock Formula class is getting ready for judging...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Stock_Formulas_1.JPG">  <BR>I was surprised that yellow Formulas outnumbered the red ones!<P>***YEAH!  Finally got PIP working!*** <BR>More pics coming...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||bHooper||08-04-2001||07:28 PM||||cool!  look at all those pretty formula's!  have you guys ever seen so many yellow one in the same place, b4?<P>i'm back, already.  call me a fool.. melinda and i drove there and back in one day (4.5 hours each way)!  we are beat, and don't have any photos to show you (we have an old fashion camera), but will tell you it was nice to see all the cars together and meet a lot of the croud!<P>we met:<BR>Phil (the car looks even nicer in person!)<BR>turbo86se- cool dude, nice car (my blackone is jealous)<BR>skitime- love those deck lid vents and removeable rear window (oops, was i not supposed to say that one?)<BR>cool87gt- dave's blue GT is sweet!<P>and of course there was the "crowd" of people that i already new:<BR>fierolisa<BR>chris moore<BR>jack cooke<BR>ed and rosie parks<BR>patrick and johnathon<P>and the guy with from raleigh with the 84 coupe w/getrag, 3.8 l, koni's and toyo proxis (he is a racing instructor at VIR).<P>we had fun (although it was a little hot), and enjoyed meeting a lot of new people!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Formula88||08-05-2001||08:15 PM||||Here's my baby reading for judging.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/F88_1.jpg">    <BR>She didn't win anything, but she looked so good sitting there, it didn't matter.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Here's LZeitgeist's Formula...He won 3rd place in Stock Formula class! (He took 1st place Stock Coupe last year at Williamsburg.  This is his first trophy at the Nationals). Way to go dude!  Notice the matching Fiero luggage.  It's form fitted for the trunk.  If it'll fit in the luggage, the luggage will fit in the trunk.  Now I gotta find me a set...<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LZ_show_r.jpg">    <P>And here is my vote for most creative engine swap!  The NOS Mouse motored Fiero brought by Phil, from Rhode Island.  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NOS_mouse.jpg">    <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> - The 3800SC in the back was sweet, too.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||08-05-2001||09:28 PM||||Whoohoo! Thanks for posting those pics, John...<P>(Last year, there wasn't a Stock Formula class, so Curry put the Formulas in with the Coupes...)<P>And yes, the 3rd in the Stock Formula class this year was a *complete* shock to me... the votes must have been *really* close, 'cuz they *all* looked really good to me, and I was sure that I'd go home empty-handed... thanks to the ones who voted for me. Thanks very much.<P><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||08-05-2001||10:20 PM||||To paraphrase Val Kilmer's Batman,<BR>"It's the luggage.  Chicks dig the luggage."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000008||Formula88||08-05-2001||10:27 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cruise.jpg"> <BR>Here's a shot of everyone lining up for the cruise through Historic Williamsburg.  It was a georgous day and beautiful weather (but, boy was it HOT).  Maybe next year, they'll have a parade permit so they won't have to try and dodge the police. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||08-06-2001||09:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>skitime- love those deck lid vents and removable rear window (oops, was I not supposed to say that one?)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the complement.  And no it is fine to say or display the window now. It was great meeting you guys. That was so funny to arrive to the hotel late in the dark and have someone I never met before yell "Hey Skitime" because they had recognized my car.  <P><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||08-06-2001||10:26 AM||||man that is one nice car! (i never asked, what color paint is that (i know it's red, but it's really nice looking!))<P>melinda and i really enjoyed meeting everyone, too bad we couldn't stay longer.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||08-06-2001||10:39 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>That was so funny to arrive to the hotel late in the dark and have someone I never met before yell "Hey Skitime" because they had recognized my car. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL!! Yup, that was me... or at least, I *think* that was me that said that as you drove up... <P>We were just hanging out late that night... me, Chris Moore, Ken Slish, Formula88, FieroLisa, and a couple others came and went...<P>Your fame precedes you!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||08-06-2001||10:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>man that is one nice car! (i never asked, what color paint is that (i know it's red, but it's really nice looking!))<P>melinda and i really enjoyed meeting everyone, too bad we couldn't stay longer.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I talked to him at the show, and he said he had it mixed to the factory red paint codes, so it's the factory hue, if not the factory paint.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||08-06-2001||10:52 AM||||Glad you and Melinda made it, Brian... it was great to see you both again... wish you could have stayed the whole weekend, but there'll be more shows... <P>||||reg||1
